cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "ISDM: Synthetic Index of Migrant Inequality (Argentina and Chile, 2015-2024)"
version: "v2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
authors:
  - family-names: Debandi
    given-names: Natalia
    affiliation: "CONICET – CIAI-UNSAM"
    email: ndebandi@unsam.edu.ar
repository-code: "https://github.com/natdebandi/ISDM-argentina-chile"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  R code that builds the Synthetic Index of Migrant Inequality (Índice Sintético
  de Desigualdad Migratoria, ISDM) from the microdata of Argentina's Permanent
  Household Survey (EPH) and Chile's CASEN survey, and the published indicators
  of Chile's National Employment Survey (ENE), 2015-2024. It reproduces every
  figure, table and number in the article "Gaps in access to rights between
  migrant and non-migrant populations in Argentina and Chile (2015-2024)".
  Version 2.0.0 corresponds to the revised version of the article (November
  2026) and includes a final notebook, in Spanish and English, with the full
  methodology, all results and 30 robustness checks.
keywords:
  - international migration
  - inequality
  - human rights approach
  - social indicators
  - composite index
  - Argentina
  - Chile
  - EPH
  - CASEN
